ale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L56-61", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Added design-system-link and generated-screens-links fields plus a mandatory-rules field"}, {"id": "day05brief_gap3_handout_stale", "label": "Gap 3: handout stale for Days 3-5, override decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L63-67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A standing leave-it-alone decision is not permanent; a later explicit instruction overrides it"}, {"id": "day05brief_curriculum_edit_split", "label": "Curriculum edit: split 46-min row into two recordings", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L71-79", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Section 12 crosses two tools (Claude Code then Claude Design); one continuous recording would be the longest asset in the course"}, {"id": "day05brief_reshape_121", "label": "\u00a712.1 reshaped: extract-then-verify", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L83-117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Hand-writing screens mixed transcription with gap-finding; transcription won because it feels finishable, starving the valuable part"}, {"id": "day05brief_bootcamp_mvp_process7", "label": "bootcamp-mvp-process.md \u00a77 (no hand-formal artifacts)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L89-92", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_askuserquestion_threshold", "label": "AskUserQuestion threshold: ask only when screen set changes", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L104-106", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_121_122_boundary", "label": "12.1/12.2 boundary: identification vs detail", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L108-110", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_slide8_rewrite", "label": "Slide 8 rewritten: five fields plus gap list", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L112-117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_slide9_added", "label": "Slide 9 added: three review passes plus visual identity", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L112-117", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_correction_pass3_actor", "label": "Correction: pass 3 named the wrong actor", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L121-164", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At pass-3 time the trainee has added nothing; Claude is the one who added screens, so the pass was asking about a flow-state that hadn't occurred"}, {"id": "day05brief_origin_field", "label": "Origin made an explicit sixth per-screen field", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L132-134", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_task_value_never_asked", "label": "Defect 2: task's actual value never elicited", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L136-148", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The highest-value moment is the trainee noticing what's still only in their head, before any design or code exists"}, {"id": "day05brief_visual_identity_rule", "label": "Visual identity rule: hex codes in priority order, never an image", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L143-146", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A palette image forces Claude to guess codes and leaves priority ambiguous from pixel proportions"}, {"id": "day05brief_two_new_slides", "label": "Two new slides: task-121-identity and task-121-gap", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L158-163", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_gap_list_interactive", "label": "Gap list closes interactively, not left as a list", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L167-189", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Claude asks about each gap immediately with suggested resolutions in the same turn, not a dead-end list"}, {"id": "day05brief_skill_md_13", "label": "designing-screens SKILL.md \u00a71.3 (gap-closing)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L178-182", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_addition_rule_test", "label": "Addition rule gets a named test (URL vs section)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L191-199", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Does it open at its own URL (new screen, needs a requirement) or is it just more content on an existing screen (a section)?"}, {"id": "day05brief_recording_121_122", "label": "Recording tasks_12.1_12.2.mp4 (6:23)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L274", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_recording_123_124", "label": "Recording tasks_12.3_12.4.mp4 (7:06)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L208-254,L278", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_eleven_screens", "label": "Real recording generates eleven screens, not one", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L213-222", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Placeholder guessed a second-screen demo; actual video shows the full inventory built out, read off Claude Code's own closing message"}, {"id": "day05brief_batch_handoff_divergence", "label": "Recording diverges: batch handoff vs per-screen rule", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L224-240", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Slide 16 prescribes a per-screen handoff; the recording batches all eleven screens then writes PRODUCT.md \u00a75 at once; per-screen rule stands because it catches a missed answer early"}, {"id": "day05brief_ffmpeg_seek_reset_pts", "label": "ffmpeg seek-resets-PTS hazard (third documented case)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L242-248,L362-370", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "trim=start:end preserves true PTS; -ss before -i resets decoded PTS to about zero, producing plausible but wrong labels"}, {"id": "day05brief_qmark_glyph_only", "label": "qmark button must contain only the glyph", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L290-296", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Putting a labelled word inside the circular badge breaks layout; grep any new qmark for more than one character"}, {"id": "day05brief_sparse_slide_blind_spot", "label": "Sparse slides are a silent failure deckAudit cannot catch", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L297-303", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "deckAudit only flags overflow, not under-using the frame; screenshot every new slide and judge density by eye"}, {"id": "day05brief_watched_exception_reearned", "label": "Watched-not-re-run exception must be re-earned per section", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L304-311", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Claude Design generation is neither one-time nor account-bound, so the default interleaved pattern applies"}, {"id": "day05brief_standing_decision_override", "label": "Standing leave-it-alone decision overridden by new instruction", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L312-317", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_subdurations_cue", "label": "Internal sub-durations are a cue for separate rows", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L318-324", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_hand_artifact_smell", "label": "Hand-produced formal artifact is a design smell", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L325-334", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Could the trainee's structured upstream data make this step unnecessary?"}, {"id": "day05brief_reversed_rule_trigger", "label": "A reversed rule needs its trigger restated, not just content", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L335-345", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Check what population a rule fires against whenever the step producing its inputs changes; the same mistake shipped again one turn later"}, {"id": "day05brief_review_vs_elicitation", "label": "Reviewing AI output and stating what only you know differ", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L346-354", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A deck can satisfy the review half completely and still omit the actual elicitation prompt entirely"}, {"id": "day05brief_existing_component_reuse", "label": "An existing component may already fit a new ask", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L355-361", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "qmark plus terms template already does what a described RTL/LTR icon would need"}, {"id": "day05brief_list_not_resolution", "label": "Producing the right list is not resolving what's on it", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L371-378", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_compressed_missing_test", "label": "Compressed sentence hides an undefined test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L379-385", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Could I apply this rule to a new case right now catches missing tests tone alone does not"}, {"id": "day05brief_designsync_corrected_1007", "label": "DesignSync mechanism corrected on slides 5, 6, 16", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L389-409", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "DesignSync uploads code component library to Claude Design and is blocked for Claude; Claude itself reads components via the DesignSync tool, not a trainee command"}, {"id": "day05brief_slide5_concept", "label": "Slide 5: three tools (Claude Design, design system, DesignSync)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L266", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_slide6_sync_limits", "label": "Slide 6: DesignSync limits (components yes, screens no)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L267,L401-404", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "day05brief_slide16_handoff_flip", "label": "Slide 16 flips default to download-only", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L405-409", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A screen's shape was never reliably obtainable from its link alone; download is now the only path"}], "edges": [{"source": "day05brief_deck", "target": "day05brief_section12", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L5-9", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "day05brief_deck", "target": "day05brief_designing_screens_skill", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L41-43", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "day05brief_gap1_day1_refs", "target": "day05brief_deck", "relation": "conceptually_related_to", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.md", "source_location": "L48-54", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "day05brief_gap2_product_md5", "target": "day05brief_section12", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "deck/day-05-brief.m